Owner |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app_int/main.py` | Add `subtract` after `add` | Developer |\n| `tests/test_main.py` | Extend import; add test function(s) for `subtract` | Developer and/or QA (whichever role the pipeline assigns tests to) |\n\nNot touched: `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, `.dark-factory*`, README, CI files.\n\n## Interface\n```\nsubtract(a: int, b: int) -> int\n```\n- Module-level function in `app_int.main`, so `from app_int.main import subtract` works (AC-1).\n- Exactly two positional-or-keyword parameters, named `a` then `b`, in that\n  order. No defaults, no `*args`/`**kwargs`, no keyword-only markers (AC-2).\n- Returns `a - b`: the first argument minus the second, not the reverse\n  (AC-3, AC-4: `subtract(3, 5) == -2`, `subtract(0, 7) == -7`).\n- Annotations: `int` on `a`, `int` on `b`, return `int` (AC-5). The module\n  already has `from __future__ import annotations`. Keep it. Annotations will\n  then be the strings `\"int\"` at runtime, which matches how `add` is written.\n  AC-5 checks the annotations in the source.\n- One-line docstring in the same style as `add`, e.g. \"Return the difference\n  of two integers (a minus b).\" Must be non-empty (AC-5).\n- No input validation and no type coercion. Behaves like `add` (smallest\n  change; nothing in the criteria asks for validation).\n\n## Tests (AC-6, AC-7)\nIn `tests/test_main.py`:\n- Change the import to `from app_int.main import add, health_check, subtract`.\n  Ruff's isort rule (`I`) needs the names in alphabetical order.\n- Add at least one test function whose name starts with `test_` and that\n  asserts on `subtract`'s return value. Recommended coverage, which matches the\n  acceptance criteria one-for-one:\n  - `test_subtract_returns_the_difference`: `subtract(5, 3) == 2`, `subtract(10, 4) == 6`\n  - `test_subtract_handles_negative_and_zero`: `subtract(3, 5) == -2`,\n    `subtract(7, 0) == 7`, `subtract(0, 7) == -7`, `subtract(0, 0) == 0`\n- Add a `-> None` return annotation to each test, like the existing tests.\n- Leave `test_health_check_reports_ok` and `test_add_returns_the_sum`\n  unchanged (AC-7).\n\n## Sequencing\n1. Add `subtract` to `src/app_int/main.py` after `add`, separated by two blank lines (PEP 8 / ruff E30x).\n2. Update the import and add the tests in `tests/test_main.py`.\n3. Run `uv run pytest -q` (AC-8) and `uv run ruff check .` (AC-9). Both must exit 0.\n4. Check that `git diff main -- pyproject.toml` is empty (AC-10).\n\n## Acceptance-criteria traceability\n| AC | Satisfied by |\n|---|---|\n| AC-1 | Module-level `subtract` in `app_int.main` |\n| AC-2 | Signature `(a, b)` with no extras |\n| AC-3, AC-4 | `return a - b` |\n| AC-5 | `int` annotations + docstring |\n| AC-6 | New tests in `tests/test_main.py` |\n| AC-7 | Existing functions/tests untouched |\n| AC-8, AC-9 | Quality gate run before finishing |\n| AC-10 | No `pyproject.toml` / lockfile edits |\n| AC-11 | Edit only `src/app_int/main.py`; no top-level `app_int/` |\n\n## Tradeoffs\n- **Tests go in the existing `tests/test_main.py` rather than a new file.**\n  This keeps all tests for `main.py` in one place. A new file would also\n  satisfy AC-6.\n- **No validation or `float` support.** The criteria specify `int`\n  annotations and only integer cases. Adding more would be scope creep.\n\n## Open questions\nNone. The only ambiguity is the `app_int/` vs `src/app_int/` path, and AC-11\nsettles it.\nEOF\ncat > $D/constraints.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"constraints\": [\n    {\"id\": \"C-1\", \"description\": \"Define subtract in src/app_int/main.py only; do not create a top-level app_int/ directory or any new source module (AC-11, task path refers to the src-layout package).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-2\", \"description\": \"Signature must be exactly subtract(a: int, b: int) -> int: two positional-or-keyword parameters named a then b, no defaults, no *args/**kwargs (AC-2, AC-5).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-3\", \"description\": \"Return a - b (first argument minus second); no input validation, coercion, or side effects (AC-3, AC-4; smallest-change decision).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-4\", \"description\": \"subtract must have a non-empty docstring in the same one-line style as add (AC-5).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-5\", \"description\": \"Do not modify or remove health_check, add, test_health_check_reports_ok, or test_add_returns_the_sum (AC-7).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-6\", \"description\": \"Do not modify pyproject.toml or uv.lock; no new runtime or dev dependencies (AC-10).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-7\", \"description\": \"Add at least one pytest test function under tests/ (preferably tests/test_main.py) that calls subtract and asserts on its return value, covering the AC-3 and AC-4 cases (AC-6).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-8\", \"description\": \"Keep the module's existing 'from __future__ import annotations' and keep imports isort-ordered (add, health_check, subtract) so ruff rule set E,F,I,UP,B passes with line-length 100 (AC-9).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"C-9\", \"description\": \"Both quality-gate commands, 'uv run pytest -q' and 'uv run ruff check .', must exit 0 before the change is considered complete (AC-8, AC-9).\"}\n  ]\n}\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('$D/constraints.json'))\" && git status --short","description":"Write design and constraints artifacts"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written the design and constraints for adding `subtract(a, b)`. One check didn't happen: the shell command I was going to use to validate `constraints.json` was denied. The file has a single required `constraints`